  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1200 PM CDT Sun Sep 27 2026\n\nNo modeling has captured the extent of the clouds and spotty\nsprinkles over a sliver of our western-third of the FA \nyesterday or today. Nevertheless, the main theme of pleasantly\ncool and dry 70s/50s will hold thru Monday. The strength of hold\nof high pressure loosens Tuesday as near surface flow shifts\nfrom the reinforcing cool northeasterlies to warmer advecting\nsoutherlies, leading to a marked warmup for the back half of the\nweek. We'll be into summer-like 80s/60s by Wednesday, with \ndaily rain chances reappearing by Thursday, and continuing into \nnext weekend. This wetter pattern may yield appreciable \ncumulative rainfall measured in 3 decimals instead of 2, and at\nleast a chance of thunderstorms appears poised to return to the\nforecast picture by week's end; that's when a cold front makes \napproach and passage, leading to another cooldown into the 70s \nheading into the weekend.",
